---
import { getCollection, render } from 'astro:content';
import { readFileSync, statSync } from 'node:fs';
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import AnalysisExplorer from '../../../components/AnalysisExplorer.astro';
import AnalysisRevisionResults from '../../../components/AnalysisRevisionResults.astro';
import AnalysisExternalSources from '../../../components/AnalysisExternalSources.astro';
import 'katex/dist/katex.min.css';
import '../../../styles/data-analysis.css';
export async function getStaticPaths() {
  return (await getCollection('archive', ({data}) => data.type === 'data-analysis' && data.status === 'published' && data.slug === 'crime-and-heat'))
    .map(entry => ({params:{slug:entry.data.slug},props:{entry}}));
}
const {entry} = Astro.props;
const {Content} = await render(entry);
const base = `/data-analysis/${entry.data.slug}`;
const revised = `${base}/data/revision-2`;
const read = (file:string) => JSON.parse(readFileSync(`public${base}/data/${file}`, 'utf8'));
const summary = read('summary.json');
const general = read('crime_model_results.json');
const revision = read('revision-2/revision_results.json');
const categories = read('categories_summary.json').categories;
const annual = read('category_aggregates.json').tables.by_year;
const reference = revision.models.find((m:any)=>m.outcome==='all'&&m.specification==='R0');
const dv = revision.models.find((m:any)=>m.outcome==='core'&&m.specification==='R0');
const signed = (value:number) => `${value<0?'−':'+'}${Math.abs(value).toFixed(2)}`;
const fmt = (value:number) => value.toLocaleString('en-US');
const dailyMB = (['daily.json','category_daily.json'].reduce((sum,name)=>sum+statSync(`public${revised}/${name}`).size,0)/1e6).toFixed(1);
---
<BaseLayout title={entry.data.title} description={entry.data.description} pageType="article" publishedTime="2026-09-24">
  <div class="analysis-page" data-analysis-study>
    <header class="analysis-intro">
      <nav class="analysis-back" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/writing/">Writing</a><span aria-hidden="true"> / </span><a href="/writing/data-analysis/">Data Analysis</a></nav>
      <p class="analysis-kicker">San Diego area · Observational analysis · Revised 24 September 2026</p>
      <h1>{entry.data.title}</h1>
      <p class="analysis-deck">Daily temperature and supplied San Diego-area arrest records, July 2018–December 2025. General findings, separate charge categories, and a domestic violence report.</p>
      <div class="analysis-actions"><a class="analysis-button" href="#explorer">Explore the data</a><a href="#revision-estimates">Revised results</a><a href="#methods">Methods and limitations</a><a href="#downloads">Research downloads</a></div>
    </header>
    <section class="analysis-finding" aria-labelledby="finding-heading">
      <div><p class="analysis-kicker">Corrected weather · Available 64-ZIP sample · 2021–2024</p><h2 id="finding-heading">The association remains inconclusive.</h2><p>The corrected reference estimate includes no association within its confidence interval (two-sided <i>p</i> = {reference.two_sided_p.toFixed(5)}). Three sensitivity tests cross 0.05 individually; none crosses 0.05 after correction across all 24 revision tests. These records do not establish that heat increases crime or violence.</p></div>
      <div class="analysis-estimate"><strong>{signed(reference.percent_change)}<span>%</span></strong><p>per 10°F higher daily maximum</p><p class="analysis-ci">95% CI {signed((reference.ci95_low-1)*100)}% to {signed((reference.ci95_high-1)*100)}%</p><small>{fmt(reference.event_count)} eligible record groups · {reference.zips} fitted ZIP areas</small></div>
    </section>
    <aside class="analysis-notice" aria-label="Revision scope"><strong>Revision scope.</strong> Corrected weather is available for 64 of 112 ZIPs following the provider’s download quota. These contain 98.5% of the original general-record sample and 98.0% of the DV sample; availability is not random. Full original results and same-sample comparisons remain below. The main analyses exclude incomplete 2025 records; no 2026 data were supplied.</aside>
    <nav class="analysis-section-nav" aria-label="Study sections"><a href="#revision-estimates">Adjusted estimates</a><a href="#explorer">Record explorer</a><a href="#weather-explorer">Daily temperature</a><a href="#methods">Methods</a><a href="#external-validation">Independent sources</a><a href="#downloads">Data &amp; sources</a></nav>
    <AnalysisRevisionResults revision={revision} originalGeneral={general} originalDv={summary} base={base} />
    <aside class="analysis-details"><h3>Category study: domestic violence</h3><p>The corrected core-DV reference estimates {signed(dv.percent_change)}% per 10°F (95% CI {signed((dv.ci95_low-1)*100)}% to {signed((dv.ci95_high-1)*100)}%; <i>p</i> = {dv.two_sided_p.toFixed(5)}), from {fmt(dv.event_count)} eligible groups and {dv.zips} fitted ZIPs. The report includes all DV sensitivity results, original comparisons, source limitations, and agency questions. Other explorer categories remain descriptive.</p><a href={`${base}/downloads/domestic-violence-and-heat-report.pdf`} download>Download the revised domestic violence report · PDF</a></aside>
    <AnalysisExplorer base={base} weatherBase={revised} weatherZipCount={revision.panel_metadata.zips} dailyMB={dailyMB} annual={annual} categories={categories} />
    <section id="methods" class="analysis-section" aria-labelledby="methods-heading">
      <div class="analysis-section-title"><span>04</span><div><h2 id="methods-heading">Methods and interpretation</h2><p>Record definitions, exposure assignment, model specification, and limits.</p></div></div>
      <article class="analysis-prose"><Content /></article>
    </section>
    <AnalysisExternalSources base={base} />
    <section id="downloads" class="analysis-section" aria-labelledby="downloads-heading">
      <div class="analysis-section-title"><span>06</span><div><h2 id="downloads-heading">Data and sources</h2><p>Aggregate data, reproducible calculations, source documentation, and unresolved questions.</p></div></div>
      <div class="analysis-downloads">
        <a href={`${revised}/revision-analysis-and-audit.zip`} download><strong>Revised analysis and audit</strong><span>ZIP · All 22 fits, 24 tests, aggregate inputs, code and verification</span></a>
        <a href={`${base}/downloads/domestic-violence-and-heat-report.pdf`} download><strong>Revised domestic violence report</strong><span>PDF · Standalone category study, methods, tables and references</span></a>
        <a href={`${revised}/data_dictionary.md`} download><strong>Revised data dictionary</strong><span>Markdown · Fields, populations, civil-day weather and exclusions</span></a>
        <a href={`${revised}/ISSUE_RESOLUTION.md`} download><strong>Methodological review response</strong><span>Markdown · Changes, sensitivity results and remaining limitations</span></a>
        <a href={`${revised}/daily_zip_civil_counts.csv.gz`} download><strong>Corrected daily counts and weather</strong><span>CSV.gz · 64 ZIPs, all available dates, daily high, mean and low</span></a>
        <a href={`${revised}/revision_results.json`} download><strong>Complete revised model results</strong><span>JSON · Estimates, intervals, tests, diagnostics and sample sizes</span></a>
        <a href={`${revised}/numerical-audit.md`} download><strong>Independent numerical verification</strong><span>Markdown · Separate calculations, findings and audit boundaries</span></a>
        <a href={`${revised}/AGENCY_CLARIFICATION_DRAFT.md`} download><strong>Agency clarification request</strong><span>Markdown · Prepared questions; not sent</span></a>
      </div>
      <details class="analysis-details"><summary>Original release and category documentation</summary><p>The original full-sample results use fixed UTC−7 weather. These files are retained unchanged for comparison and reproducibility.</p><ul class="analysis-sources">
        <li><a href={`${base}/data/general-analysis-and-audit.zip`} download>Original general analysis and audit · ZIP</a></li>
        <li><a href={`${base}/data/aggregate_downloads.zip`} download>Original shared aggregate data · ZIP</a></li>
        <li><a href={`${base}/data/audit-and-reproducibility.zip`} download>Original DV audit and code · ZIP</a></li>
        <li><a href={`${base}/downloads/domestic-violence-and-heat-original-2026-09-24.pdf`} download>Original DV report · PDF</a></li>
        <li><a href={`${base}/data/downloads/crime_model_results.csv`} download>Original general model results · CSV</a></li>
        <li><a href={`${base}/data/data_dictionary.md`} download>Original data dictionary · Markdown</a></li>
        <li><a href={`${base}/data/category_mapping.csv`} download>Charge-category classification · CSV</a></li>
        <li><a href={`${base}/data/categories_summary.json`} download>Category definitions and overlaps · JSON</a></li>
      </ul></details>
      <details class="analysis-details"><summary>Source documentation and provenance</summary><p>The arrest exports were supplied by the requester. No response letter, extraction query, or export-specific dictionary was available. Agency labels and comparisons with official reports cannot independently establish completeness. <a href={`${revised}/PROVENANCE_RESOLUTION.md`}>Source review and official documentation</a>; <a href={`${base}/data/summary.json`}>original filenames, hashes and metadata</a>.</p><ul class="analysis-sources">{summary.sources.map((s:any)=><li><a href={s.url}>{s.title}</a></li>)}</ul></details>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
